    desc: "Rarity is fixed at the species level \u2014 and rarer does not simply mean stronger.",
    detail: "Two corrections landed on August 21 that change how the whole roster should be read.<br><br><strong>Rarity is set at the species level.</strong> Every individual of a given species shares that species' rarity. There is <em>no</em> rare version of a common monster and no legendary variant of an ordinary one \u2014 if a species is Legendary, all of them are, and if it's Common, you will never roll a shiny exception. That kills a whole category of speculation about hunting commons for a lucky upgrade.<br><br><strong>Rarer is not strictly better.</strong> Bryn was specific: rares and legendaries carry a slightly better statistical allotment, but <strong>the best commons can beat middling rares and roughly match a low-end legendary</strong> on raw stat outlay. What the rarer monsters have is higher <em>potential</em> as they level, plus scarcer and higher-impact utility. Some commons carry unique traits you will need and cannot get elsewhere.<br><br>The three tiers, with the team's working definitions:<ul class=\"gp-list\"><li><strong>Legendary</strong> \u2014 pre-minted, fixed, scarce supply. Minted as <strong>NFTs</strong>. Carries traits no other tier can access. Obtained mainly through events, specific conditions and tournament wins.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong> \u2014 time-limited or event-limited availability, with final supply set by how hard players hunt. Issued as <strong>SFTs</strong>. Can appear in any hunt.</li><li><strong>Common</strong> \u2014 plain game assets with no token behind them.</li></ul>Hunting is the primary route to any monster regardless of tier.<br><br><strong>Utilities are now out, as text.</strong> The Yakkapedia names what each Genesis Legendary does, and the free-mint stream confirmed that Rare and Uncommon monsters <strong>roll their utility at random, independently of their stats</strong> — so &ldquo;rarer is not strictly better&rdquo; now has a mechanism behind it: a Common can roll the boost you need. The Yakkapedia also splits the Genesis collection into <strong>Legendary / Rare / Uncommon</strong> lines (2,750 / 4,000 / 15,000 by supply), which is where the Uncommon label enters the vocabulary. See <a href=\"?system=utilities-auras\">Utilities &amp; Auras</a> for how they work, and <a href=\"?system=genesis-legendaries\">The Genesis Legendaries</a> for the table. The numbers behind each utility are still unpublished.",
