    detail: "Resources don't go straight into your bag. They stack in a <strong>storage bin</strong> that keeps filling on its own, <strong>including while you're offline</strong>, until you tap it to collect the haul into your inventory.<br><br>The catch is the cap. Screenshots show bins counting up as <strong>84 / 120</strong> and topping out at <strong>120 / 120 MAX</strong>, with early-game bins capped at 20. Once a bin hits MAX it stops accepting, and every hour it spends full is production you never banked. That makes bin capacity, and how often you check in, a real strategic variable rather than a chore \u2014 the difference between a farm that runs all night and one that quietly stops at 2am.<br><br>A full bin is the <em>only</em> cost of being away. The free-mint stream confirmed there is no decay and no neglect penalty for not logging in &mdash; your monsters fill the bins, then stop and wait (see <a href=\"?system=upkeep\">Upkeep &amp; Degradation</a>, which is about use, not absence). Two smaller notes from the same stream: the team has moved from many bins to <strong>one bin per resource</strong>, and shops now buy resources from you. And once you hold more than one Region, expect a bin in each \u2014 the Regions post makes moving resources between them a mechanic in its own right (see <a href=\"?system=logistics\">Logistics</a>).",
